-- title:
--   Extendable prime-to-p torsion on J₀(N₀p) is inertia-invariant
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N_0$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of a fixed algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $N_0$, $p$ and $A$: a morphism $\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to the base scheme at $p$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme $X$ with a structure morphism $f$ to that base, a relative group law on $f$, and bijections between $J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, resp. the points over the residue field of $A$, and the sections of $f$ over the corresponding base points; and assume $\Lambda$ satisfies `IsJacobian`, i.e. $f$ carries the abelian-scheme property bundle, its group law is commutative, both point dictionaries are additive, the generic one is Galois-equivariant, reduction of points agrees modulo $\ell$ whenever the relevant inputs hold, and every Hecke operator is induced by an endomorphism of $f$. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data: a scheme $G$ with structure morphism $g$ to the base, a commutative relative group law, a bijection between $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ and the sections of $g$ over the generic point that is additive, Galois-equivariant and Hecke-compatible, together with the geometric hypotheses on $g$ (smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact, surjective, fibres preconnected, multiplication by each positive integer flat and surjective, generic fibre proper) and the further numerical and structural fields of that structure. Then for every $m>0$ coprime to $p$, the subgroup `O.finPts m` of $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by those $m$-torsion points $x$ whose section $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ extends to a place over $A$ (`ExtendsToPlace A Λ.σA`) is contained in `inertiaInvariantTorsion (N₀ * p) A m`, the subgroup of $m$-torsion points fixed by every element of the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$.
--
--   This is the formal counterpart of the statement that, for $m$ prime to the residue characteristic, the finite part of the $m$-torsion of the Néron model is étale over the base, so that the points extending over $A$ are unramified at $A$. It is used in the assembly of the Néron data at $p$, in [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_of_children_of_neronExtension`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.exists_jZeroNeronAtPDataOrdV22_of_children_of_neronExtension).
